    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "The Agentic Loop (Task Statement 1.1)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "How the loop works"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Send the request (with tools defined) to Claude via the API."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Inspect "
            },
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "stop_reason"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " in the response:"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": [
            {
              "spans": [
                {
                  "t": "code",
                  "v": "\"tool_use\""
                },
                {
                  "t": "text",
                  "v": " → Claude wants to call a tool. Execute the requested tool, append the "
                },
                {
                  "t": "strong",
                  "v": "tool result"
                },
                {
                  "t": "text",
                  "v": " to the conversation history, and send the next request."
                }
              ],
              "marker": "none",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "spans": [
                {
                  "t": "code",
                  "v": "\"end_turn\""
                },
                {
                  "t": "text",
                  "v": " → Claude is done. Present the final response to the user."
                }
              ],
              "marker": "none",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Repeat until "
            },
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "end_turn"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "python",
      "code": "messages = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user_request}]\nwhile True:\n    resp = client.messages.create(model=MODEL, tools=TOOLS, messages=messages, max_tokens=4096)\n    messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": resp.content})\n    if resp.stop_reason == \"end_turn\":\n        break  # final answer ready\n    if resp.stop_reason == \"tool_use\":\n        results = [execute(block) for block in resp.content if block.type == \"tool_use\"]\n        messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})  # tool_result blocks"
    },
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Why tool results go back into history"
        }
      ],
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "the model reasons about its "
        },
        {
          "t": "em",
          "v": "next"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " action based on what previous tools returned. Without appending results, every iteration starts blind."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Model-driven vs pre-configured decisions"
        }
      ],
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "the exam favors letting Claude decide which tool to call next based on context (model-driven), rather than hard-coded decision trees or fixed tool sequences — "
        },
        {
          "t": "em",
          "v": "except"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " where compliance must be guaranteed (see hooks below)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Anti-patterns (frequent wrong answers)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Parsing natural-language signals (\"It looks like I'm done\") to decide loop termination"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "dont",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Arbitrary iteration caps as the "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "primary"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " stopping mechanism"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "dont",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Checking whether the assistant returned text content as a \"completion\" indicator"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "dont",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "The "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "only"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " correct termination signal is "
            },
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "stop_reason == \"end_turn\""
            }
          ],
          "marker": "do",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Enforcement, Hooks, and Workflow Ordering (Task Statements 1.4, 1.5)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "The core exam principle"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "variant": "principle",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "When deterministic compliance is required (e.g., identity verification before financial operations), prompt instructions alone have a "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "non-zero failure rate"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ". Use "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "programmatic enforcement"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Two enforcement mechanisms in the Agent SDK:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "1. Programmatic prerequisites (gates)"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " Block downstream tool calls until prerequisites complete. Example: block "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "lookup_order"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " and "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "process_refund"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " until "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "get_customer"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " has returned a "
        },
        {
          "t": "em",
          "v": "verified customer ID"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ". This is deterministic — it cannot be \"forgotten\" the way a prompt instruction can."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "2. Hooks"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "PostToolUse hooks"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " intercept "
            },
            {
              "t": "em",
              "v": "tool results"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " before the model sees them. Use case: "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "data normalization"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " — your MCP tools return heterogeneous formats (Unix timestamps vs ISO 8601, numeric vs string status codes). A PostToolUse hook normalizes them so the agent reasons over consistent data."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Tool-call interception hooks"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " intercept "
            },
            {
              "t": "em",
              "v": "outgoing tool calls"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " to enforce compliance rules. Use case: block "
            },
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "process_refund"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " for amounts "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "over $500"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " and redirect to the human-escalation workflow."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Decision rule for the exam"
        }
      ],
      "spans": []
    },
