    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Context Management for Long Support Sessions (Task Statement 5.1)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Progressive summarization risk"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "As conversations grow, naive summarization condenses "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "numerical values, percentages, dates, and customer-stated expectations"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " into vague prose (\"customer wants a refund\" loses \"$127.43 refund for order ORD-88231 promised by Friday\")."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Fix — the \"case facts\" block"
        }
      ],
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "extract transactional facts (amounts, dates, order numbers, statuses) into a persistent structured block included "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "in every prompt, outside the summarized history"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ". For multi-issue sessions, persist structured per-issue data (order IDs, amounts, statuses) in a separate context layer."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Tool output bloat"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "An order lookup may return 40+ fields when only ~5 matter for a return. "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "Trim verbose tool outputs to relevant fields before they accumulate in context"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " (this is exactly what a PostToolUse hook can do)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Lost-in-the-middle"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
